ng absolute moves: four unchanged original H8H abs16/abs32 MOV.L groups, guarded existing0100 prefix state, original paired-word transfer order. Displacement16 memory: six unchanged H8H MOV byte/word/long load/store groups, signed16 displacement plus full ER address; guarded long prefix, no new host helper. Unsigned byte multiply: unchanged original full/partial bodies, fixed H8H m_has_mac=false (11 internal cycles plus existing host charge), no semantic helper. Word multiply remains excluded pending integer-promotion overflow review. Word multiply: selected original MULXU.W full/partial bodies with one reviewed expression adaptation in each: u16 destination operand is explicitly widened to u32 before multiplication, avoiding signed-int promotion overflow. Original reference bodies remain unmodified and run only bounded products; full-domain arithmetic is independently checked. Signed multiply: unchanged dispatch_01c0 and MULXS byte/word full/partial bodies. Guarded0xe0000 continuation accepts only signed multiply byte/word forms. Original set_nz16/set_nz32 helpers copied with class qualifiers removed, preserving all non-N/Z CCR bits. The prior MULXU.W widening remains the only two generated-body adaptations. Unsigned byte divide: unchanged DIVXU.B full/partial bodies, flat5100/ff00 dispatch. Original zero-divisor register preservation, quotient/remainder low-byte packing and divisor-based N/Z behavior retained. No word/signed division or new semantic helper enabled. Unsigned word divide: selected original full/partial bodies with explicitly u32 quotient/remainder locals replacing int. Arithmetic stays unsigned through packing, avoiding signed narrowing/packing dependence. Flat5300/ff08 dispatch. Original divisor-bit7 N and zero-divisor register preservation retained without claiming hardware verification.",
